       What twelve interviews establish, and what they do not. -->
  <section class="cst-sec" data-chrome="light" aria-labelledby="lim-h">
    <div class="cst-shell cst-shell--text">
      <h2 class="cst-h2 cst-mark cst-mark--coral" id="lim-h">what this project<br>does not prove</h2>

      <div class="cst-opts">
        <div class="cst-opt">
          <h3 class="cst-h3">nobody used it during service</h3>
          <p>Twelve interviews establish the problem well. They do not establish that this solution survives a Friday night, which is the only test that counts in a kitchen.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cst-opt">
          <h3 class="cst-h3">passive capture is an assumption</h3>
          <p>The whole architecture rests on stock drawing down accurately from POS and camera input. In practice that degrades — substitutions, comps, staff meals — and I have not designed the recovery path for when the count goes wrong.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cst-opt">
          <h3 class="cst-h3">I scoped it too wide</h3>
          <p>Inventory, pricing, sales reporting, menu management and forecasting is four products. If I restarted, I would build only the reorder loop and earn the rest.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
